course: dictionary
lesson: 6455
title: Slang and informal words
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words belong to the playground, not the classroom. «Narc» is slang, a casual word friends use when they talk to each other. You will not find it in most school reading, so context is your main clue. Read the words around it and check what fits.
explain: Imagine a playground: «Don't be a narc, we're not telling the teacher.» The speaker means that telling the teacher is disloyal, so a narc is someone who tells on other people. Swap in your meaning: «Don't be a snitch, we're not telling the teacher» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Narc can also be a verb: «She narced on her brother to Mum» means she told on him. It can also be short for «narcissist», a very vain, selfish person. Pick the meaning that fits the sentence, and check a dictionary when you are unsure.
fact: Slang is informal language used by a group of people, often friends or young people.
fact: «Narc» is slang, so you should not use it in school writing.
fact: As a noun, a narc is a person who tells on others: a snitch or tell-tale.
fact: As a verb, «to narc» means to tell on someone.
fact: In some US films, a narc is a police officer who works to stop illegal drugs.
exercise: «Don't be a narc and tell Mum about the sweets!» What does narc mean here? | A very vain, selfish person | A sweet shop worker | A police officer in a film | * A person who tells on others
exercise: Which word means the same as narc, a tell-tale? | Ancient | Cheerful | Hero | * Snitch
exercise: Should you use the slang word «narc» in a school essay? | No, because it is a number | Yes, if the teacher uses it first | * No, it is informal slang, so keep it for chatting with friends | Yes, it is a clear, formal word
test: «She narced on her brother to Mum.» What does narced mean here? | Sang | Hugged | Helped | * Told on
test: «He's such a narc, he only cares about himself.» In this sentence, narc is short for which word? | * Narcissist | Narrow | Narcotic | Narrator
exam: Ella's friend says, «Don't be a narc, Ella», when Ella wants to tell the teacher about a broken window. What is the friend warning her not to do? | Eat a snack | Play outside | * Tell on someone | Draw a picture
